{title: 653 - Lead Them, My God, to Thee}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Home}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Lead them, my [Bb]God, to [Gm]The[D]e,
[Gm]Lead [C]them to [F]Thee,
These children [Bb]dear of [Gm]min[D]e,
[Gm]Thou [C]gavest [F]me;
[C]O, [C7]by Thy [Bb]love [F]divine,
Lead them, my God, [C]to Thee;
[F]Lead them, my [Bb]God, to [Gm]The[D]e,
[Gm]Lead [C]them [C7]to [F]Thee.

Verse 2:
[F]When earth [Bb]looks bright [Gm]and fair, [D]Festive and gay,
[Gm]Let no [C]delusive snare [F]Lure them astray;
[Bb]But from temptation's [Gm]power, Lead them, [D]my God, to Thee,
[Gm]Lead them, my [C]God, to Thee, [F]Lead them to Thee.

Verse 3:
[F]E'en for [Bb]such little [Gm]ones, Christ [D]came a child,
[Gm]And in [C]this world of [F]sin Lived undefiled.
[Bb]O, for His sake, [Gm]I pray, Lead them, [D]my God, to Thee,
[Gm]Lead them, my [C]God, to Thee, [F]Lead them to Thee.

Verse 4:
[F]Yea, though [Bb]my faith [Gm]be dim, [D]I would believe
[Gm]That Thou [C]this precious gift [F]Wilt now receive;
[Bb]O take their young [Gm]hearts now, Lead them [D]my God to Thee,
[Gm]Lead them, my [C]God, to Thee, [F]Lead them to Thee.
